=> Caching system :
hello-1.0.0/
Pizza-1.0.0/


1) Create .lock
hello-1.0.0/
Pizza-1.0.0/
.lock


2) Refresh normally (without the purge_directory) but prefix new directories with '.'
hello-1.0.0/
Pizza-1.0.0/
.hello-1.0.0/
....
.lock


3.1) If there is any failure
hello-1.0.0/
Pizza-1.0.0/
.hello-1.0.0/
.lock

Remove the '.' prefixed directories
hello-1.0.0/
Pizza-1.0.0/
.lock

Finally delete the .lock to resume normal operation
hello-1.0.0/
Pizza-1.0.0/


3.2) If all goes well
hello-1.0.0/
Pizza-1.0.0/
.hello-1.0.0/
.Pizza-1.0.0/
.lock

Move '.' prefixed directories over normal ones
Don't forget to remove ALL leftover '.' prefixed directories (maybe 1 was blacklisted and now the old one is leftover)
hello-1.0.0/
Pizza-1.0.0/
.lock

Finally delete the .lock to resume normal operation
hello-1.0.0/
Pizza-1.0.0/
